        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-10T20:19:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Experimental Mutagen will have no effect on Plague Rat. As he lacks the keyword \"Rat\".</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I have always thought this was a huge oversight.&nbsp; Why else did they publish Plague Rat in the Rook City expansion, if not to call attention to how he resembles the Rats of Pike Industrial?&nbsp; I guess they just didn't want to get too experimental with the first-ever SOTM expansion.</p>",
